* zener_models.lib
* Behavioral Zener diode models for 4ms KiCad library
*
* KiCad pin mapping for all Zener symbols:
*   pin1=K, pin2=A  →  Sim.Pins = "2 1"  (A K order for SPICE D element)
*
* Model uses standard SPICE diode with Zener breakdown via BV/IBV parameters.

* BZT52C12 — 12V Zener, SOD-123, 300mW
.model BZT52C12 D (Is=1e-14 Rs=5 N=1 BV=12 IBV=1m Cjo=80p)

* Generic Zener 5.1V (useful as approximate for other low-voltage zeners)
.model ZENER_5V1 D (Is=1e-14 Rs=5 N=1 BV=5.1 IBV=1m Cjo=80p)

* Generic Zener 3.3V
.model ZENER_3V3 D (Is=1e-14 Rs=5 N=1 BV=3.3 IBV=1m Cjo=80p)

* ZPYxx — generic entry for the variable zener family (DO-41 1.3W)
* Value not known at symbol level; model is a 10V placeholder — user should
* override Sim.Name with a specific model when simulating a known Vz.
.model ZPYxx D (Is=1e-14 Rs=3 N=1 BV=10 IBV=1m Cjo=100p)
